@engagement = http://localhost:4002

### Redeem coins for a store item (workflow steps 6-7)
# Inside the POST: order recorded (stock and limit decremented, price and reward frozen), then a synchronous
# coin reserve in payments. The casino reward is issued afterwards by the sweeper through the adapter port,
# with our idempotency key redeem:<id>. The POST never calls the casino.
# The answer is always 202 Accepted (the redemption is not finished), including a replay of the same key.
# The Idempotency-Key header is required and has 8 to 128 characters.
# {{player_token}} is the launch session token (02).
# @name redeem
POST {{engagement}}/v1/redemptions
Authorization: Bearer {{player_token}}
Idempotency-Key: redeem-0001-player-77
Content-Type: application/json

{ "item_id": "0190...-item" }

# Response (shape from the contract, not captured):
# HTTP/1.1 202 Accepted
# A player never sees the history: it holds operator reasons, so the player view always has "history": [].
# {
#   "id": "0190...-redemption", "item_id": "0190...-item", "price": 40,
#   "status": "pending", "state": "RESERVED", "attempts": 0,
#   "casino_reference": null, "failure_reason": null,
#   "history": [],
#   "created_at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.000Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.100Z"
# }

### The same redemption as the operator sees it: reasons and the full history
# The operator token needs the engagement audience (see 01).
GET {{engagement}}/v1/operator/redemptions/{{redeem.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{operator_engagement_token}}

# Response (the history causes are captured from scripts/demo.sh; the rest is shape from the contract, not captured):
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# { "id": "0190...-redemption", "status": "pending", "state": "RESERVED", "failure_reason": null,
#   "history": [ { "from": null, "to": "REQUESTED", "cause": "order_placed", "at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.000Z" },
#                { "from": "REQUESTED", "to": "RESERVED", "cause": "reserved", "at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.100Z" } ],
#   "...": "..." }

### Not enough coins: the player sees it at once (decision D-8)
POST {{engagement}}/v1/redemptions
Authorization: Bearer {{poor_player_token}}
Idempotency-Key: redeem-0002-player-12
Content-Type: application/json

{ "item_id": "0190...-item" }

# Response (captured from scripts/demo.sh):
# HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict
# {"message":"not enough coins","code":"insufficient_funds"}
# Stock and per-player limit are put back; no casino call was made.

### Out of stock
